<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maluku Islands</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Moluccas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Maluku Islands, or Moluccas, are an archipelago in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, historically known as the Spice Islands. They were the original source of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cloves">cloves</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nutmeg">nutmeg</a> and mace, which were highly prized in global trade. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> seized control of the spice trade there in the seventeenth century, making it a cornerstone of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>'s economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maluku-islands.jpg" alt="Maluku Islands" width="320" height="353" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lencer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maluku_Islands_en.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
